# Adding Thumbnails to Media Mentions

This guide explains how to add or update thumbnails for media mentions on the website.

## Media Mentions Structure

Media mentions are stored in `_data/media_mentions.yml` with the following structure:

```yaml
- title: "Article Title"
  url: https://example.com/article
  publisher: Publisher Name
  date: YYYY-MM-DD
  type: Article/Video/Conference Talk/etc.
  language: en/ru
  thumbnail_url: /data/articles_thumbnails/filename.webp
  website_logo_url: /data/webstie_logos/logo.png
```

## Image Requirements

- **Location**: 
  - Thumbnails → `data/articles_thumbnails/`
  - Website logos → `data/webstie_logos/`
- **Format**: WebP format preferred for thumbnails, PNG/SVG for logos
- **Dimensions**: 520×297 pixels (16:9 aspect ratio) for thumbnails
- **Naming Convention**: 
  - Thumbnails → `publisher-YYYY-MM-DD.webp` 
  - Logos → descriptive name reflecting the source (e.g., `fedor-youtube-channel.png`)
- **Quality**: Use 100% quality for best appearance

## Step-by-Step Process

### 1. Check the existing thumbnails and logos

```bash
ls -la data/articles_thumbnails/
ls -la data/webstie_logos/
```

### 2. For YouTube videos, fetch the thumbnail

```bash
# Get thumbnail URL
curl -s "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=VIDEO_ID" | grep -o 'og:image" content="[^"]*' | cut -d\" -f3

# Download thumbnail
curl -s -o /tmp/youtube-thumbnail.jpg "THUMBNAIL_URL"
```

### 3. Analyze your source image

```bash
identify -format "%wx%h" /tmp/youtube-thumbnail.jpg
```

### 4. Process the image

For best results with YouTube thumbnails:

```bash
# Standard resize with proper 16:9 aspect ratio
magick /tmp/youtube-thumbnail.jpg -resize 520x297^ -gravity center -extent 520x297 -quality 100 data/articles_thumbnails/youtube-YYYY-MM-DD.webp
```

This command:
- Resizes the image to fill the 520×297 frame (`^` operator)
- Centers the content (`-gravity center`)
- Crops to exact 520×297 dimensions (`-extent`)
- Sets maximum quality (`-quality 100`)
- Saves in WebP format

### 5. Verify the processed image

```bash
# Check dimensions - MUST be exactly 520x297 for proper display
identify -format "%wx%h" data/articles_thumbnails/youtube-YYYY-MM-DD.webp

# Check quality
identify -verbose data/articles_thumbnails/youtube-YYYY-MM-DD.webp | grep Quality

# Check file size
ls -la data/articles_thumbnails/youtube-YYYY-MM-DD.webp
```

### 6. Update the YAML file

Edit `_data/media_mentions.yml` to add both the thumbnail and logo URLs:

```yaml
- title: "Your Video Title"
  # ... other properties ...
  thumbnail_url: /data/articles_thumbnails/youtube-YYYY-MM-DD.webp
  website_logo_url: /data/webstie_logos/appropriate-logo.png
```

## Troubleshooting

### Background Issues

If the thumbnail has unwanted background elements:

```bash
# Make background transparent (useful for some cases)
magick source-image.jpg -background none -fuzz 10% -fill none -draw "color 0,0 floodfill" -resize 520x297^ -gravity center -extent 520x297 -quality 100 output.webp

# Alternative: Force a specific background color
magick source-image.jpg -background "#000000" -resize 520x297^ -gravity center -extent 520x297 -quality 100 output.webp
```

### Image Aspect Ratio Issues

If your source image has a very different aspect ratio than 16:9:

```bash
# First extend to proper aspect ratio with padding
magick source-image.png -gravity center -background "#000000" -extent 1280x720 -resize 520x297 -quality 100 output.webp
```

### Visual Verification

Always check the final result on the website to ensure:
1. The thumbnail displays correctly without stretching/squeezing
2. The image is centered properly on the subject
3. No unwanted elements appear at the edges

### Logo Handling

When using custom logos:
1. Use descriptive filenames that indicate the source
2. Maintain consistent styling with other logos
3. Ensure proper transparency for non-rectangular logos

## Example Workflow

```bash
# Check source image
identify -format "%wx%h" /Users/kirill/Downloads/source-image.png
# 1252x710

# Process image to correct dimensions with high quality
magick /Users/kirill/Downloads/source-image.png -resize 520x297^ -gravity center -extent 520x297 -quality 100 data/articles_thumbnails/publisher-2023-01-01.webp

# Verify the result
ls -la data/articles_thumbnails/publisher-2023-01-01.webp
identify -verbose data/articles_thumbnails/publisher-2023-01-01.webp | grep Quality

# Update the YAML file with the new thumbnail reference
# Edit _data/media_mentions.yml
``` 